<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Owain the Bald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1018</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Owain Foel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Owain the Bald, in Welsh Owain Foel, was the last known king of Strathclyde, the Brittonic kingdom of the Clyde valley. He may have fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malcolm-ii-of-scotland">Malcolm II of Scotland</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carham">Battle of Carham</a> around 1018 and died about then. After him the kingdom was absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> during the 11th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/owain-the-bald.jpg" alt="Owain the Bald" width="320" height="109" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Owain_Foel_(Cambridge_Corpus_Christi_College_139,_folio_94v)_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
